                  <provenance type="#e" cert="low" source="980"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_100">Cambridge,
                        Cambridgeshire. Gonville Hall</orgName><p>A long erased note following the
                        table of contents, fol. 1*v. A reagent has been used. Probably this note
                        accounts for the entry by J. A. Herbert in the class-catalogue that this MS
                        belonged to St Peter's or Gonville Hall in 1474.</p></provenance>
               <provenance type="#e" cert="low" source="1008"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_106">Cambridge,
                        Cambridgeshire. Peterhouse (Collegium Sancti Petri)</orgName><p>A long
                        erased note following table of contents on fol. 1*v. A reagent has been
                        used.</p><p>Like Egerton 889, this table of contents is numbered and headed
                        'Contenta in hoc volumine sunt ista', in the hand of Roger
                        Marchall.</p><p>Fol. 1r: 'Iste liber est scriptus anno domini 1272. .
                     .'</p></provenance>
